WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:06.000
Speaker 1: Let's go next to Alex from Des&nbsp;
Moines, Iowa. Alex, you're on the air.&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.560
Speaker 3: Hey, David, thanks for having me. I&nbsp;
have been shocked, as I imagine you are, at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:19.040
amount of media coverage that has not included&nbsp;
George Bush's name. Yes, repeatedly regarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.000
Afghanistan. Yes. And I'm kind of stunned and&nbsp;
I'm wondering if you see it this way as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.320
I've been thinking about all the events that&nbsp;
have unfolded, and I'm left with this impression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:38.400
which is we got into this mess. Was George Bush&nbsp;
accomplished the one clear goal that we had?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:47.760
And then it seems every president there left after&nbsp;
were. Well, to be fair, George Bush didn't have an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.920
accomplishment. Obviously, we had to wait until&nbsp;
Obama was president to get that accomplishment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.960
and then from that point forward, no one knew&nbsp;
what to do. I have a hard time blaming Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.320
or for even that matter, Trump in this case&nbsp;
